's hot temper and loner may be serious. B's nasty remarks also serious. C's communication difficulty also serious. A's not open to new ideas may affect adaptability.\n\nWe need to weigh. Perhaps Candidate A's leadership and anticipation of danger could be valuable, but health (unhealthy eating) may affect reliability. Not open to new ideas is adaptability issue.\n\nMaybe we could ask for more info on professional communication for D and B. But we have some: B makes nasty remarks, wrong tone. D is hot temper, loner. So both have crew issues.\n\nWhich candidate has the least crew issues? Possibly Candidate A: leadership qualities, but also show-off and not open to new ideas. Not sure about communication. No explicit negative communication. So maybe A is better? But health and adaptability concerns.\n\nWe could argue that Candidate A's ability to anticipate dangerous situations and leadership outweigh the adaptability concerns, and health can be managed. So we could shift vote to A.\n\nBut we need to be careful: we must reference current discussion and provide evidence. Let's propose that after reviewing all, I think Candidate A is the best overall because of anticipation, technical insight, leadership, and no explicit severe crew cooperation issues (only not open to new ideas). The health issue (eats unhealthily) is less immediate safety risk than hot temper or nasty remarks.\n\nThus we can change vote to Candidate A.\n\nWe need to include evidence: \"anticipates dangerous situations\" (decision quality), \"very good leadership qualities\" (crew cooperation), \"sees complex connections\" and \"excellent spatial vision\" (technical competence). Also note concerns: \"not open to new ideas\" (adaptability) and \"eats unhealthily\" (reliability). Then argue that compared to D's hot temper and loner, A's concerns are less safety-critical.\n\nThus we can propose vote for A.\n\nWe must also note that we still need to discuss B and C further, but we can give provisional vote.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON with vote \"Candidate A\"."}
